From 290160b29ba0330ee6c767f5894c4b0355813323 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: sardi-dev <134648583+sardi-dev@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 20:12:37 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 17/25] Add the Silvershard Mines battleground

The battleground had a template row and a start location but no class, so
it could not be queued for or played. Three mine carts ride rails to the
depots, the team standing next to a cart keeps it, and a cart that reaches
a depot gives its keeper 150 points. Each kept cart also gives one point
per second, the first team to 1600 wins. The two track switches change
where the east and the north cart end up.

Adds the queue type, the scoreboard column, the cart paths, the spell click
rows of the track switches and the strings of the messages. Capturing
(97388) and the dummy it triggers (97372) call the battleground through the
new Unit overload of EventPlayerClickedOnFlag. The achievements of the map
are left out, their criteria types are not implemented.

Based on Legends of Azeroth 5.4.8.
